                <div data-article-body="true" data-track-component="article body" class="c-article-body">

                    
                    <section lang="en"><div class="c-article-section" id="Abs1-section"><div class="c-article-section__content" id="Abs1-content"><h3 class="c-article__sub-heading" data-test="abstract-sub-heading">Abstract</h3><p>The object of this research was to determine whether <i>Ammi visnaga</i> extract, which would be utilized in traditional herbal medicine, exhibited antifungal activity against <i>Aspergillus glaucus</i> on the liver, kidney, lung, and brain tissues of experimental animals (albino male rats) by physiological and biochemical variables. The whole number of animals was divided into five groups (six) for each group of animals. (1st) group: control group; (2nd) group: <i>A. glaucus</i> spore suspension (HD); (3rd) group: <i>A. visnaga</i> extract + <i>A. glaucus</i> (HD); (4th) group: <i>A. glaucus</i> spore suspension (LD); (5th) group: <i>A. visage</i> extract + <i>A. glaucus</i> (LD). By looking at lipid peroxidation (MDA content), antioxidant enzyme activities such as superoxide dismutase (SOD), and catalase (CAT) as oxidative stress markers. A considerable increase in LPO and a decrease in the activation of antioxidant enzymes (catalase, superoxide dismutase) in treated groups compared to controls were found to indicate oxidative stress. Urea, creatinine, total protein, aspartate transaminase (AST), and alanine transaminase (ALT) were all measured in the blood serum. The serum enzymes ALT and AST were found to have lower concentrations, but serum urea and creatinine concentrations were higher. Furthermore, mammalian toxicity was investigated in terms of DNA damage generated in treated rat tissues compared to control tissues. According to these findings, <i>A. visnaga</i> extract possesses antioxidant properties in rats and may be effective in the treatment of oxidative stress in a variety of chronic diseases.</p></div></div></section>

                    

                    
    


                    
                        
                            
